# Interpretation framework\
\
A claim such as *\'93scarcity is characterized by a reward-rate-dominated mode\'94* should require individual-level evidence:\
\
1. Individual models predict held-out later behavior better than useful baselines.\
2. A substantial proportion of individuals show reward rate as the largest dominant-mode loading.\
3. Those eigenvectors are reasonably stable under within-person block bootstrap.\
4. Spectral-radius estimates are reasonably stable.\
5. The pattern is not driven by a small number of participants.\
\
If those conditions fail, the appropriate statement is narrower:\
\
> The pooled operator contains a reward-dominated direction, but individual organisms exhibit heterogeneous local dynamics.\
\
